WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.460
If you build on Cloudflare, your usage is spread across products, plans and accounts.

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:07.710
usageflare brings it into one place.

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:17.009
It connects to each of your Cloudflare accounts, and reads usage across the four areas you pay for: compute, storage and databases, AI, and messaging.

00:00:17.159 --> 00:00:22.310
Every number is measured against your plan's allowance, and forecast to the end of the month.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:28.110
So you can see what's blocked, what's already billing, and what's about to run out, before it happens.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.749
Cloudflare bills by resource, but you think in projects.

00:00:33.899 --> 00:00:39.340
Filter for anything without a tag, pick resources from any account, and tag them in one go.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:44.754
The tags land on the resources in Cloudflare too.

00:00:44.904 --> 00:00:48.830
Then group by tag and product, to see what each project uses.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.760
Now, where is the money going?

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:59.079
Ask it as a column: each resource's share of the bill.

00:00:59.229 --> 00:01:02.750
It's checked as you type, and the answer lands on every row.

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:07.347
Then keep that answer in sight.

00:01:07.497 --> 00:01:13.190
Put the chart or number you check every day on your dashboard, and it's there every time you open it.

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:27.604
usageflare.

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:28.651
Every account.

00:01:28.801 --> 00:01:29.570
Every limit.

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:30.360
One gauge.
